From b2928e3fbf3e3d1701bc374ef9cd7fb8b164c856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:27:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Video: named camera moves, the frames people publish in, and
 seeds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every AI clip KOKAO generated received the same seven-word motion suffix
("Subtle natural motion, cinematic.") — a sensible default and a hard
ceiling, because there was no way for a user to ask for a crash zoom, an
orbit, or a whip pan. This adds the vocabulary, the frames, and the
reproducibility control that were missing around it.

Camera moves
  A curated catalog of named presets (lib/videoGen/motionPresets.ts),
  each a label plus the prompt sentence it compiles to. The sentence is
  the whole feature: our providers take plain text, not an effect id, so
  each preset names the move, its framing consequence and its pacing.
  A preset WINS over the built-in instruction rather than joining it —
  "subtle natural motion" and "crash zoom" cannot both be obeyed.
  Prompt Kit governance still owns the default, which is what an
  unpicked job gets, so a job without a preset renders byte-identically
  to before.

  Presets are set per job and overridable PER SHOT on a storyboard
  scene, which is the thing a single prompt box cannot do: shot 1 can
  crash zoom while shot 2 holds locked off.

Aspect ratios
  Adds 4:5, 4:3, 3:4 and 21:9 to the existing three. 4:5 is the sharp
  omission for a social product — it is the Instagram feed ratio, and it
  outperforms square. No model renders 4:5, so a ratio the chosen model
  cannot produce is requested as the nearest one it CAN (nearest by
  crop loss, ties broken on orientation, never on floating-point noise)
  and cover-cropped to the exact frame by the normalize pass that
  already runs. The delivered file always matches what was asked for.

Seeds
  An optional per-job and per-scene sampling seed, so the same prompt
  renders the same way twice and a shot the user liked survives a
  re-roll of its neighbour. Sent only to model families whose schema
  carries a seed: Replicate 422s on unknown input keys and a 422 costs
  the tenant a paid video unit, so Veo and MiniMax never see it.

New endpoint: GET /ai/video-motion-presets returns the catalog grouped
for a picker. Ids are permanent, so clients cache it.

No migration: every field is optional on the existing options and scene
JSON, and absent means exactly the old behaviour.

Verified: pnpm run typecheck clean across all packages; api-server
videos suite 92/92 and the videoGen suites green; web 838/838; spec
lints and the codegen drift check is clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
